[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is one ticket. Read report by report, it holds more than one problem,
and the queued parser fix closes only one of them. Every number on this page is computed from the
export.

<Callout kind="warn">
One ticket per problem. Each one is filed on its own.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {links} />

### `parser`

The shared parser reads every date month first, and the tenants write the day first, so day and
month swap.

<ReportQuote id="R-41200" />

### `hint`

The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says,
and the form reads it in the tenant's order, day first. Only reports sent through that form. The
parser fix does not touch it: the form has to print the tenant's order.

<ReportQuote id="R-41241" />

### `shift`

The date moves by one day, not a day/month swap. The desk read these reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`). It looks like a date-only value passed through a time zone. The parser fix
does not touch it.

<ReportQuote id="R-41344" />
<ReportQuote id="R-41236" />

## Why the merge hid them

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line, and the problems
arrive with the same subjects (listed under the table). Its consequences say engineering would split
them later.

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for `parser`.
2. Route `hint` to the booking-v3 form owners.
3. Route `shift` to whoever turns booking dates into invites.
4. Replace decision 0001 with a record that merges on what a report describes, not its subject.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
